What the MIT grant does not cover
---------------------------------

**The map this app draws.** The WMS tiles it requests are rendered from hexagon
meshes derived from CShapes 2.0 and CShapes-Europe, which are CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
Those tiles, and any image made from them, are adaptations under that licence:
attribution, non-commercial use only, share-alike.

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

So the code here may be reused freely, including commercially, but not while
pointed at a Demscore hex-map WMS endpoint. Point it at a tile service built
from permissively licensed geometry and only the MIT terms apply.

**`config/attribution_sources.json`** is a register of other people's citations
and licence statements, reproduced so the app can display them. It is factual
reference material about third-party works, not a contribution of this project.

**`assets/codebooks/*.pdf`** are the data providers' own documents (V-Dem, QoG,
REPDEM), redistributed unchanged and belonging to them. Each dataset requires
citation as a condition of use; the citations are in the app's "Sources &
licences" dialog.

**`assets/images/demscore-logo.svg`** is Demscore's mark, used with permission
and not licensed onward. The panel background photograph is by Adrien Ledoux via
Unsplash, under the Unsplash Licence.
